            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0464" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9588: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-23T13:00:00+09:00">August 23, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 23—1:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. Department’s No. 159, August 21, 11 p.m., Tsingtao. Department’s
                    instructions received this morning were carried out in a formal note to the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs which I delivered to <pb facs="0465" n="458"
                        xml:id="pg458"/> the Vice Minister shortly after noon. No alterations were
                    made in the Department’s text. The Vice Minister made no comment except to say
                    that the matter would be studied.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
